      "interpretation": {
        "evidence_refs": [
          "s0:0000161A:instruction",
          "s0:00001622:instruction",
          "s0:000028DE:instruction",
          "s0:000028E2:instruction"
        ],
        "reason": "The initializer writes LONG seeds95901143/28731549 to app+60/+64. advance_shared_random_state and its inline point-field/retry copies read both, rotate the first LONG, subtract7 from its low WORD, XOR with the second, and store the old second/new result back. These are the two evolving shared PRNG state components, not pointer fields or the separate six-byte/314159 startup seeds. Byte/WORD perturbations remain aliases.",
