    "regression": "With native A6=ExecBase and a same-offset app name, the old renderer printed the app name despite a known TDNestCnt typed access. The unbound case failed before and passes after; explicit use-site binding still wins."
  },
  "shared_fix": "Explicit/manual use-site names retain priority. A resolved native typed field then takes precedence over an automatically inferred global app-slot coincidence. No target address or field-name recognizer, source-string patch, or new analysis engine.",
  "facts": [
    "Original sourceBC34 loads A6 from absolute4; BC3A increments byte+127; BC3E reloads SysBase before SuperState. Canonical A6 struct_ptr ExecBase at BC3A yields the generated NDK field TDNestCnt (task-disable nesting), not IDNestCnt or app storage. The seed is instruction-scoped, not a new control-flow entry.",
    "App+60/+64 are the two LONG components of the existing shared random generator: fixed seeds95901143/28731549, ROL.L3, low-WORD SUBQ7, XOR, old-second/new-result stores. Canonical scalar regions now name them shared_random_state_a/b. Partial byte/WORD perturbations remain aliases; the separate six-byte/314159 initialization state is not conflated.",
    "The KB library-to-ExecBase association is absent while the generated ExecBase field map exists. Use existing scoped canonical typing; do not silently re-extract the 3.1 KB from the available 2.0 assembly snapshot or invent a global mapping."
  ],
